{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310592,"nonce":"dXYFoSiXDaRsz1WJqUZKBd0FmJE=","title":"Compiler bug FIXED (1d82346c, 2026-06-21): an untyped empty array literal `var a = [];` was eagerly Array\u003cDynamic\u003e and never refined, so ...","message":"Found porting the Q8_K quantizer for the Phase-4 qmatmul ([[project_haxe_q4_dot_phase3]]); I first mis-attributed it to \"Array\u003cFloat\u003e set/get truncates on wasm\" — WRONG, corrected here.\n\n- `var lit = [1.5, 2.75, 3.14]` (float literals) → CORRECT native + wasm.\n- `var set = [0.0, 0.0]; set[0] = 1.5;` → CORRECT.\n- `var typed:Array\u003cFloat\u003e = []; typed.push(0.0); fillFloat(typed);` → CORRECT.\n- **`var a = []; a.push(0.0); fillFloat(a);`** (untyped empty literal) → **WRONG**: wasm reads 0 (f64→i32 truncation), native reads 4575657221408423936 (the f64 bits reinterpreted as i64). Both targets store the float into an Int-typed array.\nSo the trigger is ONLY the untyped empty `[]` literal: its element type locks to Int and is NOT refined by a later `push(floatExpr)` or by being passed to an `Array\u003cFloat\u003e` parameter. Reference/Int element arrays are unaffected (Int is the inferred default; pointers fit i32/i64 either way).\n\nReal footgun, but NARROW. It bites only code that builds a float array from an untyped empty literal then fills it (silently-wrong values, worse on wasm = 0). nue is NOT hit in practice: its `var x = []` sites hold Int token ids (`var ids = []`) or `{name, tensor}` parameter structs (`var ps = []`), never floats (grep confirmed, 9 sites). Any new float-accumulation code (samplers, norms, logits) using `var a = []` WOULD be hit.\n\nAnnotate the element type: `var a:Array\u003cFloat\u003e = []`, or seed with a float literal `[0.0]`. (The Q4 qmatmul test sidestepped it differently — Q8_K block scales in a Bytes via setDouble/getDouble — which also works; annotation is the simpler fix.)\n\n- try_bind falls back to LOWERING Call/Field/Index/New args (e.g. `a.push(x.getFlat(i))`, `p.push(new Box())`) for their type when the cheap syntactic peek can't; symbol stays tracked so a later peekable push can bind it (\"until getFlat's return type says otherwise, or another push does\"). GENERAL: binds Float/Int/String/Bool/class, not Float-only.\n- W0110 normal warning when an untyped `[]` was USED but stayed uncertain (Dynamic): \"type of array literal can not be inferred at assignment, this would fall back to Array\u003cDynamic\u003e; annotate `var a:Array\u003cT\u003e = []` for deterministic behavior at runtime\". Only fires if it STAYS uncertain (a later peekable push clears it). Plumbing: ast_lowering take_empty_array_warnings → compilation.rs collected_diagnostics (Warning, UNGATED — not emit_safety_warnings) + pipeline result.warnings; main.rs renders W-prefixed compile warnings in `run` (was Error-only); E-coded safety warnings (E0382) keep their own display (filter W-prefix to avoid double-print).\n\nast_lowering.rs: track symbols declared as untyped empty array literals (`empty_array_inferred` set, populated in the Var arm). At the first `arr.push(e)` (Call arm) / `arr[i] = e` (Assign arm), `try_bind_inferred_array` peeks e's type (`peek_ast_expr_type`: literals, in-scope idents, arithmetic — earlier statements already lowered so idents resolve) and rewrites the symbol's type to Array\u003cT\u003e via update_symbol_type, BEFORE the receiver lowers — so the receiver + all later refs route through the typed (f64) push/get path. Unpeekable args (method-call results, etc.) keep Array\u003cDynamic\u003e (no regression; the alloc is type-agnostic elem_size=8, only push/get ROUTING keys on element type — hir_to_mir.rs:9516). Suite 146 passed. The Q4 qmatmul's Bytes-for-d workaround is now unnecessary (Array\u003cFloat\u003e would work) but harmless.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_empty_array_literal_float_inference` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}